 "conclusion": "The hot-expert kernels stream on persistent grids: the decode MoE pipeline (select, gate/up, down, combine) takes 13-16% less time at width 4 and 6-11% less at width 1, with bit-identical decode-path logits. The combine waits for the CPU tier beside hot_down, the GR norm/down kernel preloads its inject rows and row scales, and a verify step with MTP drafts folds GDN/PLE state beside the drafts. Coding chat decoded 3.5% and 9.3% more tokens per second (7-8% less time per speculative round); the corpus cases moved within run-to-run variance except the 32K prompt (+9.1%).",
